# Series of the Orange Pi 5 board patches, applied after the ARM64, SoC and OS series.
#
# The NVMe personality is this board's own; the evb10-* patches are the EVB10's, copied unchanged (see VENDORED.md: they hold the userland
# hook, the Data volume, the SystemOS union mount and the console tweaks every RK3588 board of this port needs, and live in the EVB10 repository
# only because that board came first). Their order is the EVB10's, because their context lines depend on it.

# The NVMe drive in the M.2 slot: personality of NativeNvme (package/Rk3588Nvme), next to the SoC's one for the eMMC host
orangepi5-nvme-personality.patch
# Why a process went away (evb10-ps=N)
evb10-exit-trace.patch
# mmap(PROT_EXEC) of the owner's directory of programs and libraries
evb10-mmap-grant.patch
# User-stack frame-pointer chain of the threads of named processes (evb10-bt*)
evb10-thread-sample.patch
# Userland hook: Data volume, SystemOS union mount, owner test program, GPU add-on
evb10-userland-mounts.patch
# Mirror of the console on the frame buffer (vc_mirror=1) and -v text mode
evb10-vc-mirror.patch
